      "heading": "Fill in the blanks using the words in the word bank.",
      "text": "The [frequency] of a wave is the number of waves passing a point each [second]. It is measured in [hertz]. The [wavelength] of a wave is measured in metres. If the frequency of a wave increases and its speed stays the same, its wavelength [decreases].",
      "showWordBank": true
    },
